# How many times can you fold paper in half?
subtitle: "Guess the record for folding paper in half, then see how a student beat the 'seven folds' myth, and why doubling makes each fold harder."

## How many times can you fold paper in half?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: gallivan
      title: 'How to Fold Paper in Half Twelve Times: An ''Impossible Challenge'' Solved and Explained'
      authors: B. Gallivan
      year: 2002
      finding: in January 2002 she folded a roughly 1.2 km strip of toilet paper in half twelve times in one direction, and derived the length each fold needs
    - id: stmarks
      title: St. Mark's School team breaks paper-folding record
      authors: The Boston Globe
      year: 2011
      url: http://archive.boston.com/news/local/articles/2011/04/10/st_marks_school_team_breaks_paper_folding_record/
      finding: students folded toilet paper 13 times in MIT's Infinite Corridor

    icon sheet size 110 set twemoji x 160 y 590 icon_look picture of "page facing up" hidden true
    scale folds cites ["gallivan"] x 150 y 470 width 700 unit folds min 0 max 20 value 12 ticks 4 hidden true
    text old "old 'limit'" #8f887c x 395 y 545 font_size 34 hidden true
    icon roll size 130 set twemoji x 270 y 290 icon_look picture of "roll of paper" hidden true
    text km "1.2 km of paper" #2f6b8f x 600 y 290 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon moon size 120 set twemoji x 250 y 290 icon_look picture of "crescent moon" hidden true
    text moon_t "42 folds: past the Moon" #b5482e x 580 y 290 font_size 44 hidden true
    text t13 "2011: 13" #8f887c x 740 y 548 font_size 34 hidden true
    path mark13 #8f887c points [[605,482],[605,528]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    path mark7 #8f887c points [[395,520],[395,478]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true

    card title "How many folds in half?"

How many times can you fold a sheet of paper in half?
    draw sheet folds

    ask "What is the most times one piece of paper has been folded in half? Click on the line." on folds store f default "7"
        right: Close: you said {f}. The record on a single sheet is {f.true}, set in 2002.
        wrong: You said {f}. The record on a single sheet is {f.true}, set in 2002.

For years, people said seven folds was the limit.
    draw mark7 old

Then, in 2002, a high-school student in California, Britney Gallivan, set out to prove them wrong.
    highlight folds

She worked out how much paper each fold would ne (@draw roll km@)ed, and found a roll of toilet paper about one point two kilometres long.

Then she folded it in half twelve times, in the same direction.
    highlight km

    erase roll km

Nine years later, students from Saint Mark's S (@draw mark13 t13@)chool taped toilet paper down a corridor at MIT and managed thirteen.

Why is it so hard? Each fold doubles the layers: one, two, four, eight, sixteen, thirty-two.
    shape st0 #2f6b8f shape rect x 180 y 217.5 width 56 height 5 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl0 "1" #2f6b8f x 180 y 242 font_size 28
    shape st1 #2f6b8f shape rect x 260 y 220 width 56 height 10 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl1 "2" #2f6b8f x 260 y 247 font_size 28
    shape st2 #2f6b8f shape rect x 340 y 225 width 56 height 20 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl2 "4" #2f6b8f x 340 y 257 font_size 28
    shape st3 #2f6b8f shape rect x 420 y 235 width 56 height 40 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl3 "8" #2f6b8f x 420 y 277 font_size 28
    shape st4 #2f6b8f shape rect x 500 y 255 width 56 height 80 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl4 "16" #2f6b8f x 500 y 317 font_size 28
    shape st5 #2f6b8f shape rect x 580 y 295 width 56 height 160 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.35
    text stl5 "32" #2f6b8f x 580 y 397 font_size 28

After twelve folds, there are four thousand and ninety-six.
    text lay2 "12 folds: 4,096" #2f6b8f x 790 y 330 font_size 40

And each fold needs far more length than the last, because the paper must wrap around an ever thicker stack.
    highlight st5

    erase st0 stl0 st1 stl1 st2 stl2 st3 stl3 st4 stl4 st5 stl5 lay2

Keep doubling a sheet a tenth of a millimetr (@draw moon moon_t@)e thick, forty-two times, and the stack would reach past the Moon.
